  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef took an examination two times. In the first attempt, he scored XXX marks while in the second attempt he scored YYY marks. According to the rules of the examination, the best score out of the two attempts will be considered as the final score.\n\nDetermine the final score of the Chef.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers XXX and YYY — the marks scored by Chef in the first attempt and second attempt respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the final score of Chef in the examination.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "0≤X,Y≤1000 \\le X, Y \\le 1000≤X,Y≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n40 60\n67 55\n50 50\n1 100",
        "output": "60\n67\n50\n100",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: The best score out of the two attempts is 606060.\nTest Case 2: The best score out of the two attempts is 676767.\nTest Case 3: The best score out of the two attempts is 505050."
      }
    ]
  },
